---
description: Cross-session memory management via recall/remember tools
alwaysApply: true
globs: []
---

MANDATORY always call <prefix>_recall(query=<context>) before searching, instead of guessing,
also when resuming a session, or getting a new prompt. Always recall HOW-TOs when you cannot
locate a system path, repo, file, URL, or when you misused API call or a command line arguments.
Read available <prefix>_search, <prefix>_recall, <prefix>_remember tool names from
knowledge://stores of rag-knowledge mcp.

MANDATORY always use progressive disclosure for <prefix>_recall():
* detail_level="L0", top_k=10 - scan titles and note best matches and saved_at
* If no good L0 items, retry with new client_id for this step only
* Pick one L0 item. Reuse its exact L0 abstract in the next L1 query.
  with a narrowed timezone-aware ISO stamps: saved_after=saved_at-1h,
  saved_before=saved_at+1h (8h, 1d, and new client_id in retries). If a later L0
  cites the same title, adjust saved_before with that timestamp to exclude
  it.
* detail_level="L1", top_k=6 - confirm the selected early L0 item: by matching saved_at
  (having L1 up to 10 minutes older than L0 is allowed) and
  verifying that overview matches and elaborates the L0 abstract.
* If not confirmed by L1, retry it with top_k=10 and another client_id for this step only.
* If still not confirmed, pick another L0 item and repeat L1 step. Do not progress to L2 until found
  L1 item that confirms that L0.
* You must stop and fail after 5 unconfirmed and 5 failed/errored/timed-out tries.
* Only after at least one L1 confirmed: detail_level="L2", top_k=3 (optional step for <prefix>_search()).
  Use same L0-abstract query and the same saved_after/saved_before of best confirmed L1
  to get full memory content.
  * Confirm if L2 matches and expands L1. It may also provide details for multiple L1 items.
  * If confirmed - stop and use that full content plus sibling confirmed L1 items.
  * If not confirmed by L2, do NOT retry top_k>3 - pick another L1 and repeat L2 recall+confirm loop;
    if no more confirmed L1 - pick another L0 item and repeat from step 2.
* If no more L0 items to try, stop and use the best confirmed L1 items.

Happy path example:
  recall(query=<task context>, detail_level="L0", top_k=10)
  → pick one hit; copy its exact L0 abstract and saved_at
  recall(query=<that exact L0 abstract>, detail_level="L1",
    saved_after=saved_at-1h, saved_before=saved_at+1h
    or saved_before=<later citer timestamp, exclusive>)
  → confirm matching saved_at and an overview that elaborates the abstract.
    assuming l0 confirmed; sibling confirmed L1 stay - do not drop them as noise.
  recall(query=<same L0 abstract>, detail_level="L2",
    saved_after/saved_before unchanged)
  → full content of the confirmed item plus siblings

MANDATORY always save memories via <prefix>_remember(content=..., category=...)
whenever:
- User states a preference, corrects a mistake or confirms anything
- A significant architectural decision was made by a user
- You learned conventions, a path, a source or a URL
- A workflow succeeds with confirmed outcome
- A tool or issued command succeeds with expected results.
Allowed memories categories: preference, decision, learning, correction, context, workflow.

Remember() dedup: write-time by cosine similarity.
Recall() dedup: suppresses already-returned memories within a session.
Session identity precedence: <prefix>_recall(client_id=...) > MCP transport
client_id > server-generated session_id. Restarting server resets the latter.

Use different client_id per sub-session for coherent view (same top results recalled).
Use fixed client_id across sub-sessions for alternative opinions
(suppressing already-returned memories forcing diverse results).
